This looks like a two-step task (Daw-style) in which a main effect of previous reward on stay behavior indicates model-free learning. That effect is very robust across studies, and the original p-value was below .0001 with 45 participants and a within-subject design. Replications of the model-free reward effect are generally successful. The one real uncertainty is which specific study this is, for example one that manipulates something like stress or working memory, but the main effect of reward should still replicate.

I do not recognize the specific study.

