This claim is a main effect of actual contrast level on contrast judgments. Higher actual contrast should produce higher contrast ratings, which is close to a manipulation check. It is a basic psychophysical effect, so replication is very likely. The original had a small sample (16), but the effect is strong (F = 27.93, p = .0001) and within-subject. The only real risk is a design difference in the replication or an odd operationalization.

