This is Knobe's (2003) side-effect effect, the chairman/environment harm and help vignettes. It is one of the most replicated findings in experimental philosophy. Knobe's original effect was large (82% vs. 23%). Replications, including cross-cultural ones and the Many Labs-style replications in xphi, have consistently found the asymmetry. The original sample of 78 is modest, but the effect is large enough that a replication should be well powered.

The remaining risk is a replication that changes the wording or population, but a direct replication should succeed.


