This looks like Kidd & Castano (2013), "Reading literary fiction improves theory of mind." Its original experiments were widely questioned, and the claim here is the Experiment 3 replication of the literary versus popular fiction comparison on the RMET. Later work, including Panero et al. (2016) with multiple replications and a Many Labs-style replication, found no significant effect. The replication in this setting was probably a Camerer et al. (2018) SSRP study, which found failure for Kidd & Castano Study 1. The original here has p = .04 with N = 69, which is weak evidence, and the prior plausibility of the claim is low.

I do recognize the original paper, but I do not recall the specific outcome of this Experiment 3 replication, so I am relying on the broader failure pattern.

